==English==

===Pronunciation===
*:Rhymes: [[Rhymes:English:-ɛrɪk|-ɛrɪk]]

===Proper noun===
'''Derek'''

# A male [[given name]] of English and Old German origin meaning ''power of the tribe'' ... possible origin ''Theodoric'' <ref>
[http://www.behindthename.com/php/view.php?name=theodoric Behind the Name Article]</ref> or ''ruler of the people''. In recent years it has occasionally been used as a family name.

===Alternative forms===
Derek takes various forms in many languages: Darek, Darrick, Darriq, [[Del]], Dereck, Deric, Derick, Derik, Deriq, Derk, Derreck, Derrek, [[Derrick]], Derrik, Derryck, Derryk, Deryck, Deryk, Deryke, Dirk, Dirke and Dyrk. <ref>
[http://www.thinkbabynames.com/meaning/1/Derek Think Baby Names Article]
</ref>
Related names are Dedrick, Derry, Jerrick, Darroch and Dietrich. 

